In `packages/app-store/_utils/oauth/parseRefreshTokenResponse.ts`, `minimumTokenResponseSchema` is defined as:
```ts
z.object({
  access_token: z.string(),
  [z.string().toString()]: z.number(),
  [z.string().optional().toString()]: z.unknown().optional(),
});
```
Both computed property names are derived from calling `.toString()` on Zod schema objects, which yields the same string key (typically `"[object Object]"`), so the second overwrites the first and the intended “any numeric property is expiry” contract is not implemented. Also, because `z.object()` strips unknown keys by default, `safe

